the family of archie battersby have been  told his life support is due to be  withdrawn tomorrow morning after their  legal fight to move him from hospital to  a hospice came to an end  a last-ditch plea to the european court  of human rights to intervene in the case  was rejected following a high court  ruling that he must remain at raw london  hospital in whitechapel east london the  case has been in the courts for several  weeks  in june a judge first ruled that  archie's life support treatment should  stop  with doctors saying it was highly likely  that he was brain stem dead  archie's parents disputed this and were  then given permission to appeal against  the ruling at the court of  appeal judges there then rule that  archie's case should be reconsidered at  the high court  that judge ruled that doctors could  lawfully stop providing life support  treatment saying its continuation would  delay the inevitable  after appeals from archie's parents the  united nations requested that the 12  year old was to be kept alive while it  considered his case  but the supreme court dismissed the  family's application to appeal the  decision to remove life support with  treatment due to be withdrawn yesterday  morning  the family then applied to the european  court of human rights to intervene  but it said it would not interfere with  previous rulings by national courts  the family submitted an application to  the high court yesterday  seeking permission to move archie to a  hospice where his life support would be  removed  however today the high court judge ruled  that it wasn't in archie's best interest  to move him to a hospice the family then  turned to the court of appeal to  overturn the decision  and the echr decided again on a second  appeal that it wouldn't interfere in the  case  let's speak to our correspondent shiman  freeman powell who's outside the  hospital where archie is being treated  and shimano it looks as though this very  sad story is uh coming to an end  it really does and it has been an  extremely traumatic time for the  appearance of archie battersby ever  since april when they found him  unconscious at their home and since then  they've been enthralled in legal  challenges that you've just talked us  through trying initially to keep archie  battersby's life support ongoing but it  did become quite clear on wednesday that  the all legal options as uh to keep his  life support ongoing had been exhausted  so then the battle moved to trying to  get artie battersby transferred to a  hospice because uh holly dance archie's  mum had made it clear that she would  like for archie to spend his last days  in a peaceful environment and not in a  hospital which is often known for the  chaos and noise however it does seem  that that is not going to happen earlier  today the parents of archie battersby  had gone to the high court and the  courts have appealed to try and get  archie's move to a hospice but they  ruled that it was not in his best  interest to do so saying that his  condition was so unstable that even with  the best medical equipment that that  move wouldn't be in archie's best  interest and we're now hearing that  archie battersby's life support machine  will be turned off at 10 am tomorrow  morning we do have a statement from a  spokesperson for the campaign group  christian concern which is supporting  archie's family they've said that all  legal routes have now been exhausted the  family are devastated and are spending  precious time with archie right from the  very beginning archie's parents have  made it clear that they would not stop  fighting until the very end and no one  can dispute that that is exactly what  they've done they've been to the high  court they've been to the courts of  appeal they've been to the supreme court  and they've also been to the european  court for human rights but it does seem  that this story has now sadly come to an  end
 

